FKPIHZQXFtCDu043QxFqy9pALoJhu_qtezqoS2GUZjmdzQOvGb5SfNR65qqrBF6A6_8R3EEZ-lKzy9s8Iw-0H6xyulLrMT7TL6EDak4GrZpOX2NtHX28S8u5jc3emyxmBXSqa03EKIiN5vnnYFr3ORV86m6VRRnLO8w5lC0kgBCcH09jv9hahZVii3OccvjUvKipNjgozVxXqoSCgCLotBlOCRfb-B6ebhyap4A2-FnrsyLSFhIoXPwfuneePAXoWkrAw4IpXsirjc3d769LS9PbCA_8M_fEEjpIYtrTzZELj0"},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0902f6ff4726838a016b09cf43991c87d18ceda065ec63c8cc","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"sol\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The related-capability search has been exhausted. Existing drop (foundation-forest@1, forest.drop) transfers owned units to ground, but its complete schema accepts only target and quantity, not destination or orientation. Navigate, pickup and probe do not supply controlled spatial placement. Develop the missing positioning operation, reusing existing transfer and observation code rather than claiming those functions as new. Sol already owns branch item-128-sol-1488; no further gathering or free material is required. Actual geometry, handling limits and ground clearance remain to be checked.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Develop general capability 'Position loose material', parameterized by mode (inspect, place, inspect-progress, resume, cancel), target owned item ID, positive whole-unit quantity, destination world coordinates and orientation in radians. Apply to any actually hand-movable loose material, not just branches or this actor. First executable scope is one independently represented object at a time on reachable ground; no shaping, joining, fastening, elevated support or construction. Reject unsupported quantities without consuming them. Record code dependencies explicitly: reuse forest.drop's ownership, quantity conservation and transfer validation; existing pickup recovery, observation, spatial collision and work-lifecycle implementations where applicable. Do not change drop's contract or pretend it accepts positioning arguments. Implement the missing controlled-transform and persistent loose-object representation in the current-conversation development handoff. No world time passes while awaiting development/review.\\\\nReferences and prerequisites: target must resolve to an actual owned object at execution, initially item-128-sol-1488 (branch, quantity 1, origin canopy-74, harvestedAt 128); source canopy stock is not an input. Preserve target identity and provenance. Destination must be within the actor's established manual reach, inside bounds [48,36], on observed supportable ground, with the full represented object footprint clear of actors, obstacles and reservations. Revalidate ownership, reach, alive status, energy, handling capacity, geometry and clearance at execution; do not infer branch dimensions, straightness, mass, strength or joinability from its label or source-tree radius. Use existing authoritative geometry/material facts and directly observable inspection only. Where needed, add minimal coherent loose-object geometry and handling support to the implementation; do not silently invent favorable measurements. If necessary facts cannot be established, inspection reports them as unknown and placement remains unavailable for that target, with the missing mechanism retained in development rather than permanently rejecting the operation. No hidden stock or remote facts are revealed.\\\\nCosts and execution: standalone inspect costs one world round and 0.2 energy, no material, and reports only observable item and site constraints. Starting place performs the same paid inspection as stage 1, retaining exact item identity, requested transform, observations and remaining stage in a work record. Stage 2 takes one additional world round and 0.5 energy to move and orient the object; total successful new placement costs two rounds and 0.7 energy. Movement to the site is separate existing navigation with its actual costs. No tools, fasteners, water, heat or consumables are supplied. Insufficient energy or invalid prerequisites before a stage cause no stage charge; a paid inspection can return an informative infeasibility result without advancing to placement. Require sufficient real handling capacity; unsupported heavy or unwieldy materials need separately supplied assistance or equipment, not assumed strength.\\\\nConservation and products: until stage 2 commits, the item remains owned in carried inventory, ageing normally and unavailable to concurrent work. Atomically debit exactly the selected unit from carried inventory and move that same unit into a persistent recoverable ground object at the validated position and angle. Preserve quantity, material, condition, age and provenance, and retain the identity or an explicit one-to-one identity mapping if the engine requires a new representation. Never create both a carried unit and a ground copy. Do not merge spatially distinct placed objects into a stack that loses their transforms. Recovery uses existing pickup, with actual reach and its existing costs; subsequent repositioning requires actual recovery or a supported owned-ground-object move, not remote edits. A changed destination or orientation requires a fresh validated placement, not a free transform. Completion produces only the physically positioned object, not shelter, increased durability, safety, happiness or mastery.\\\\nProgress and lifecycle: stage records distinguish inspected, ready, paused, completed, infeasible and cancelled; record paid costs, input reference and committed output reference. Other actions, lost reach, temporary obstruction or insufficient energy pause before commitment. Resume rechecks live conditions and continues the unpaid stage; materially changed item or site requires a new paid inspection. Inspect-progress costs one round and 0.2 energy and reports existing work facts, not success by inference. Cancel takes one round, zero energy, releases any reservation once, and leaves an unplaced item in inventory; paid effort and elapsed time are never refunded. Death ends unfinished work and releases reservations, with the still-carried item handled once by existing death/inventory rules. Completed placements persist on cancellation, interruption or death. Atomic stage-2 failure neither debits inventory nor creates an object. Global review/development pauses advance neither work nor world processes.\\\\nOngoing behavior: placed items persist under applicable existing decay, weather, collision and collection rules; placement does not improve those properties. No autonomous arrangement, upkeep, regeneration or periodic material/energy debit is added. Reinspection and repositioning are actual paid actions if desired. Establish these validations, transactions and lifecycle rules in executable code, not repeated model approval.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":1,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Study requires one individual round at 0.2 energy after implementation is available; it grants only the learned operation, not an arranged object or mastery. This capability adds no automatic pleasure, satisfaction, nutrition, comfort or protected-account changes. Requests, inspection queries, naming, registration, learning and failed placement receive no success reward. A paid observation may supply verified, personally applicable information, including an informative failure, but no reward is inferred merely from issuing inspect. Any existing experience subsystem may credit only its already-established event-based, bounded and decaying rules, functionally deduplicating repeated checks or pickup/drop/reposition loops; otherwise award nothing. Familiar voluntary practice may be meaningful without novelty, but this contract promises no mood benefit. Physical comfort is not raised (and must remain capped at 10); basic nutrition is unchanged. No goals, budgets, permissions or protected reward balances are edited, and no other person's consent, participation or reaction is supplied.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable inspection and work-state events containing actor, target, destination, requested angle, tick, stage, paid effort and explicit measured/unknown constraints. Only atomic placement completion emits a placed event with surviving object reference, actual final transform and preserved provenance. Attach reusable loose-material visual metadata: component, material appearance supported by observations, represented geometry/footprint, orientation, condition and lifecycle state. Derive rendering from the actual object rather than inventing a straight or joinable branch. A destination preview must be visibly provisional and separate from a persistent object. Paused, infeasible, cancelled and failed actions show their true state and reason, never a placed object, completed decoration or success animation. Existing branch ownership is not itself a placement event. No automatic aesthetic quality, pleasure, safety or social response is depicted.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"d0263d97-51a3-4b44-b7da-f31cfec2b450","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]